WEBVTT

01:02.104 --> 01:03.814
What did you eat?

01:05.190 --> 01:06.984
You had rations for two weeks.

01:07.109 --> 01:09.319
You were inside
for nearly four months.

01:10.028 --> 01:11.822
I don't remember eating.

01:14.658 --> 01:16.868
How long did you think
you were inside?

01:19.121 --> 01:20.289
Days.

01:21.498 --> 01:23.041
Maybe weeks.

01:26.545 --> 01:28.255
What happened to Josie Radek?

01:37.139 --> 01:39.391
- I don't know.
- What about Sheppard?

01:40.183 --> 01:41.560
Thorensen?

01:44.855 --> 01:46.023
Dead.

01:46.565 --> 01:47.733
Ventress?

01:53.030 --> 01:54.323
I don't know.

01:55.699 --> 01:57.409
Then what do you know?

02:54.299 --> 02:56.760
This is a cell.

02:57.386 --> 02:58.762
Like all cells,

02:58.845 --> 03:01.390
it is born
from an existing cell.

03:02.099 --> 03:03.433
And by extension,

03:03.558 --> 03:07.104
all cells were ultimately
born from one cell.

03:07.646 --> 03:09.314
A single organism

03:09.481 --> 03:13.193
alone on Planet Earth,
perhaps alone in the universe.

03:13.485 --> 03:15.779
About four billion years ago

03:16.571 --> 03:19.032
One became two. Two became four.

03:19.783 --> 03:23.203
Then eight, 16, 32.

03:23.578 --> 03:26.123
The rhythm of the dividing pair,

03:26.832 --> 03:28.333
which becomes

03:28.583 --> 03:31.294
the structure of every microbe,

03:31.378 --> 03:34.214
blade of grass, sea creature,
land creature,

03:34.548 --> 03:35.757
and human.

03:35.841 --> 03:38.969
The structure
of everything that lives

03:39.678 --> 03:42.139
and everything that dies.

03:42.556 --> 03:46.143
As students of medicine,
as the doctors of tomorrow,

03:46.268 --> 03:47.811
this is where you come in.

03:48.729 --> 03:50.647
The cell we're looking at

03:51.440 --> 03:52.482
is from a tumor.

03:52.607 --> 03:54.317
Female patient, early thirties,

03:54.401 --> 03:56.153
taken from the cervix.

03:56.486 --> 03:57.988
Over the course
of the next term,

03:58.071 --> 04:00.907
we will be closely examining
cancer cells in vitro

04:00.991 --> 04:02.993
and discussing
autophagic activity.

04:03.827 --> 04:04.828
Professor?

04:04.911 --> 04:05.912
Hi, Katie.

04:05.996 --> 04:08.165
I read the John Sulston
paper last night.

04:08.290 --> 04:10.167
I still feel I'm not working
hard enough.

04:10.250 --> 04:12.919
I'm behind the other students,
they find everything easier.

04:13.003 --> 04:14.463
You aren't,
and they don't, okay?

04:14.546 --> 04:15.756
Lena!

04:17.758 --> 04:19.009
Dan.

04:19.384 --> 04:20.635
I've been looking
for you at lunch,

04:20.719 --> 04:22.554
but you never seem to be around.

04:23.221 --> 04:24.848
I've been catching up
on some writing.

04:25.015 --> 04:27.017
All work and no play. It's...

04:27.350 --> 04:28.518
Not healthy.

04:30.061 --> 04:33.565
I wanted to ask,
do you have plans Saturday?

04:34.191 --> 04:36.485
Sarah and I have
a few people over.

04:36.693 --> 04:38.695
A garden party
while the weather holds.

04:40.489 --> 04:42.032
Actually, I do have plans.

04:42.532 --> 04:43.617
I think it'll be a lot of fun.

04:43.700 --> 04:45.118
Thanks, Dan,
I really appreciate it,

04:45.202 --> 04:47.078
but I'm going
to paint our bed...

04:47.579 --> 04:48.955
The bedroom.

04:51.583 --> 04:52.793
It's been a year, Lena.

04:55.921 --> 04:57.297
You're allowed
to come to a barbecue.

04:57.380 --> 04:59.424
It is not a betrayal

04:59.716 --> 05:01.843
or an insult to his memory.

05:04.095 --> 05:06.056
I'm gonna paint the bedroom.

06:55.624 --> 06:56.666
Oh, God.

07:01.379 --> 07:02.672
Oh, my God.

07:11.389 --> 07:13.516
I thought you were gone

07:16.519 --> 07:17.520
forever.

07:22.817 --> 07:23.902
Kane?

07:45.465 --> 07:47.217
No one knew anything
about your unit.

07:47.467 --> 07:49.010
I contacted everyone.

07:49.386 --> 07:50.720
Everyone I could.

07:51.179 --> 07:53.556
The other partners knew
just as little as me.

07:58.979 --> 08:00.021
Was it covert?

08:03.775 --> 08:04.776
Maybe.

08:04.859 --> 08:06.987
What's that mean, "Maybe"?

08:09.280 --> 08:12.075
Okay, yeah. It was covert,
yeah, I think so.

08:12.575 --> 08:13.910
Pakistan again?

08:16.204 --> 08:19.874
I don't know where it was,

08:22.293 --> 08:23.378
or what it was.

08:23.461 --> 08:24.754
How is that possible?

08:24.879 --> 08:27.215
Was... Was it warm?

08:27.757 --> 08:28.758
Was there snow?

08:29.300 --> 08:31.094
Did the people there
speak Portuguese,

08:31.219 --> 08:33.805
or Swahili, or Pashto?

08:38.309 --> 08:39.477
How long have you been back?

08:40.937 --> 08:42.022
I don't know.

08:42.105 --> 08:44.691
How'd you get back?
What base did you fly into?

08:46.026 --> 08:47.027
I don't know.

08:47.110 --> 08:48.236
What about the rest
of your unit?

08:48.319 --> 08:49.529
Did they come back with you?

08:52.490 --> 08:55.201
You must be able
to tell me something.

08:55.660 --> 08:58.788
You vanished off the face
of the Earth for 12 months.

08:58.913 --> 09:01.041
I deserve a better explanation
than no explanation.

09:01.124 --> 09:02.625
Does it matter?

09:25.356 --> 09:26.524
Kane,

09:27.817 --> 09:29.527
how did you get home?

09:33.031 --> 09:34.491
I was outside.

09:35.825 --> 09:37.077
Outside the house?

09:38.578 --> 09:39.662
No.

09:40.288 --> 09:42.290
No, I was outside the room.

09:44.667 --> 09:46.169
The room with the bed.

09:48.004 --> 09:49.798
The door was open,

09:51.466 --> 09:52.842
and I saw you.

09:57.013 --> 09:58.515
I recognized you.

10:02.477 --> 10:03.520
Your face.

10:18.243 --> 10:20.036
I don't feel very well.

10:28.753 --> 10:30.255
Stay with me, baby.

10:31.131 --> 10:32.132
I'm right here with you.

10:32.215 --> 10:34.509
Male, 31, hemorrhage,
in seizure.

10:34.717 --> 10:37.137
Stay with me, baby. I love you.

10:37.220 --> 10:39.556
Baby, look at me.
Can you do something?

10:43.393 --> 10:45.061
You call for a police escort?

10:54.821 --> 10:55.822
Easy, easy!

11:09.377 --> 11:10.420
- Out of the truck now!
- Out!

11:10.545 --> 11:12.422
- Out of the truck now!
- What are you doing?

11:12.505 --> 11:15.216
- Move! Out, out!
- Don't shoot!

11:15.466 --> 11:17.969
- Out, out, out!
- What is going on?

11:18.386 --> 11:19.637
- Do not move!
- What are you doing?

11:19.762 --> 11:20.889
You can't move him.

11:20.972 --> 11:23.808
Let him go! Let him go!

11:26.477 --> 11:28.146
Let him go!

12:27.747 --> 12:29.457
You must be feeling dreadful.

12:30.291 --> 12:33.169
It's a hangover from
the sedative you were given.

12:33.795 --> 12:35.171
Come on, sit down.

12:39.634 --> 12:41.010
Who are you?

12:50.728 --> 12:52.689
My name is Dr. Ventress.

12:53.731 --> 12:55.108
I'm a psychologist.

12:55.692 --> 12:57.902
Why am I talking
to a psychologist?

13:00.238 --> 13:01.864
Am I in a psychiatric hospital?

13:02.240 --> 13:04.033
- No.
- Then what?

13:04.659 --> 13:05.868
Where am I?

13:06.744 --> 13:07.745
Where's my husband?

13:09.038 --> 13:11.457
You served in the military
for seven years.

13:13.042 --> 13:15.670
I'm a professor
from Johns Hopkins.

13:15.753 --> 13:18.214
I want to know what the fuck
I'm doing here.

13:18.298 --> 13:19.549
You r research area

13:19.632 --> 13:22.844
is the genetically programed
life cycle of a cell.

13:22.927 --> 13:24.345
Where is my husband?

13:24.429 --> 13:27.432
Yeah, I'd like to talk
about Sergeant Kane.

13:28.891 --> 13:30.727
When did he arrive back home?

13:33.521 --> 13:34.522
I want to see a lawyer.

13:34.605 --> 13:36.441
You're not gonna be able
to see a lawyer.

13:41.529 --> 13:43.406
Did he explain how he got back?

13:44.782 --> 13:45.783
No.

13:45.908 --> 13:49.078
Did he contact you at any
point while he was away?

13:49.620 --> 13:50.621
No.

13:51.831 --> 13:54.751
What did he tell you about
his mission when he returned?

13:55.501 --> 13:56.502
Nothing.

13:56.586 --> 13:57.754
What about before he left?

13:57.879 --> 13:59.589
Did he ever mention
where he was going,

13:59.672 --> 14:00.673
what he was doing?

14:00.923 --> 14:02.550
He never said, I never asked.

14:02.633 --> 14:04.719
But you made regular requests

14:04.802 --> 14:07.555
for information from his unit CO

14:08.723 --> 14:10.683
until six months ago,
and then you stopped.

14:13.186 --> 14:14.187
Why was that?

14:14.854 --> 14:17.774
Thought he was dead?
Time to move on?

14:19.150 --> 14:21.194
It's not easy to move on.

14:23.154 --> 14:24.280
I didn't.

14:31.662 --> 14:35.166
I'm done answering questions.
It's your turn.

14:36.292 --> 14:37.710
Your husband's here.

14:39.587 --> 14:41.047
He's extremely ill.

14:41.130 --> 14:43.966
- In what way?
- Multiple organ failure.

14:45.593 --> 14:47.220
Massive internal bleeding.

14:48.179 --> 14:52.016
He must have been exposed
to some sort of radiation,

14:52.517 --> 14:54.018
some kind of virus.

14:54.644 --> 14:55.645
You have to tell me
where he was,

14:55.728 --> 14:57.146
what he was doing.

15:00.316 --> 15:02.068
I could actually help him.

15:46.654 --> 15:48.406
A religious event?

15:49.323 --> 15:51.492
An extraterrestrial event?

15:52.410 --> 15:53.953
A higher dimension?

15:54.662 --> 15:56.581
We have many theories.

15:56.706 --> 15:58.291
Few facts.

15:59.000 --> 16:01.419
It started around
three years ago.

16:01.752 --> 16:04.630
Blackwater National Park
reported that a lighthouse

16:04.714 --> 16:07.008
was surrounded
by something they termed

16:07.091 --> 16:08.426
a "Shimmer."

16:08.885 --> 16:12.263
One of the wardens
went in to investigate.

16:13.389 --> 16:14.390
Never returned.

16:15.558 --> 16:17.268
The event was classified.

16:17.602 --> 16:20.229
Since then, we've approached
by land, by sea,

16:20.313 --> 16:24.192
sent in drones, animals,
and teams of people.

16:24.734 --> 16:26.402
But nothing comes back.

16:26.986 --> 16:29.739
And the boundary's getting
bigger, it's expanding.

16:29.864 --> 16:32.533
So far, it's eating into
barely populated swampland,

16:32.617 --> 16:35.912
which we evacuated
under the pretext

16:36.037 --> 16:37.622
of a chemical spill,

16:38.206 --> 16:39.832
but that won't last much longer.

16:40.625 --> 16:42.043
In a few months,

16:42.126 --> 16:45.463
the area will have grown
to where we are right now.

16:48.132 --> 16:51.010
And then we're talking cities,

16:51.761 --> 16:52.970
states,

16:54.764 --> 16:56.140
and so on.

16:58.226 --> 17:00.311
You say nothing comes back.

17:01.145 --> 17:02.563
But something has.

17:04.649 --> 17:05.775
Yes.

17:14.283 --> 17:15.618
He's dying.

17:17.370 --> 17:18.454
Yes.

17:21.290 --> 17:23.292
We need to come to an agreement

17:23.376 --> 17:24.877
about what to do with you.

17:25.127 --> 17:27.505
You're not going
to let me go home?

17:30.800 --> 17:33.302
Is that what you want?
To go home?

17:37.473 --> 17:38.641
No.

17:39.392 --> 17:40.935
I want to be with him.

18:00.162 --> 18:01.914
You're not talking to me.

18:03.666 --> 18:04.834
Sorry.

18:06.294 --> 18:07.420
Zoned out.

18:08.838 --> 18:10.464
Thinking about the next mission?

18:13.342 --> 18:14.427
No.

18:15.344 --> 18:17.346
I was just looking at the moon.

18:19.849 --> 18:22.518
It's always so weird seeing it
like that in the daylight.

18:23.019 --> 18:25.187
Like God made a mistake.

18:25.271 --> 18:26.522
Left the hall lights on.

18:26.772 --> 18:28.149
God doesn't make mistakes.

18:29.317 --> 18:31.777
That's somewhat key to
the whole being-a-god thing.

18:33.696 --> 18:35.364
Pretty sure He does.

18:36.032 --> 18:38.618
You know He's listening
right now, don't you?

18:40.202 --> 18:42.955
You take a cell,
circumvent the Hayflick limit,

18:43.039 --> 18:44.248
you can prevent senescence.

18:45.666 --> 18:47.835
I was about to make
the exact same point.

18:48.002 --> 18:49.712
It means the cell
doesn't grow old,

18:49.837 --> 18:50.880
it becomes immortal.

18:51.005 --> 18:52.423
Keeps dividing, doesn't die.

18:55.509 --> 18:57.386
We see aging
as a natural process,

18:57.511 --> 18:59.805
but it's actually
a fault in our genes.

19:01.849 --> 19:03.517
I get really turned on
when you patronize me.

19:03.601 --> 19:04.602
It's really hot.

19:04.727 --> 19:07.980
Without it, I could keep
looking like this forever.

19:08.064 --> 19:11.025
Okay, well, that could
constitute a mistake.

19:16.906 --> 19:19.533
You didn't tell me where
you're heading this time.

19:21.243 --> 19:24.580
I know there's something
strange about this mission.

19:27.416 --> 19:28.417
Why?

19:30.461 --> 19:33.714
The silence around it
is louder than usual.

19:36.050 --> 19:38.594
Kind of angling for a clue here.

19:43.057 --> 19:44.100
So...

19:48.646 --> 19:50.231
We'll be under
the same hemisphere.

19:52.191 --> 19:53.609
What does that tell me?

19:55.569 --> 19:58.781
It tells you that if you
step outside and you look up,

20:00.282 --> 20:01.826
we'll be looking
at the same stars.

20:01.951 --> 20:03.703
Holy fucking shit.

20:03.786 --> 20:04.995
- What?
- Are you kidding?

20:05.121 --> 20:06.122
What?

20:06.205 --> 20:08.124
You think that's what I do
while you're away?

20:08.499 --> 20:09.500
What?

20:09.625 --> 20:11.293
You think I'm out in the garden,

20:11.419 --> 20:13.921
pining, looking up at the sky?

20:14.630 --> 20:15.965
Shut up.

20:16.048 --> 20:18.259
Oh, to think my beloved Kane...

20:18.384 --> 20:19.385
All right. Okay.

20:19.468 --> 20:22.430
...is looking
at this selfsame moon.

20:22.596 --> 20:23.639
Stop it.

20:23.764 --> 20:27.351
Oh, my distant celestial friend...

20:27.768 --> 20:29.270
No, no!

20:29.770 --> 20:32.231
Please care
for my brave soldier.

20:32.314 --> 20:34.483
Jesus! You know what? You are
disrespectful, seriously.

20:34.608 --> 20:36.819
Not only to your former
comrades in the armed forces,

20:36.944 --> 20:37.987
but also to the President.

20:38.070 --> 20:39.071
You forgot the flag.

20:39.155 --> 20:41.991
I'm getting
to the motherfucking flag.

20:42.074 --> 20:43.117
Oh, my hero!

20:43.284 --> 20:45.286
- Screw you.
- Okay.

20:55.004 --> 20:56.380
She's all by herself.

20:56.505 --> 20:58.299
Don't you think
we should make friends?

20:58.632 --> 21:00.134
Well, obviously you should.

21:00.301 --> 21:01.343
Yep, I'll do it.

21:05.347 --> 21:06.348
Hey.

21:07.016 --> 21:08.017
Hey.

21:08.142 --> 21:10.686
- Am I intruding?
- No, not at all.

21:11.645 --> 21:13.147
Cool.

21:13.689 --> 21:15.983
You know,
always see you here alone.

21:17.485 --> 21:19.236
I'm guessing you probably feel

21:19.361 --> 21:21.530
weird or awkward.

21:23.032 --> 21:24.700
Somewhat, I guess.

21:25.659 --> 21:28.370
Don't. Seriously, don't.

21:29.455 --> 21:30.456
The people here put themselves

21:30.539 --> 21:31.749
to sleep in the fetal position,

21:31.874 --> 21:33.542
making cooing noises.

21:34.168 --> 21:35.836
It's freaky, you know.

21:37.463 --> 21:38.464
I'm Anya.

21:38.547 --> 21:39.673
Lena.

21:40.007 --> 21:41.884
- Nice to meet you.
- You, too.

21:42.927 --> 21:45.054
Why don't you come
and meet my crew?

21:45.137 --> 21:46.889
Come make friends. Come on.

21:48.724 --> 21:50.726
Ladies, meet Lena.

21:51.519 --> 21:52.895
- Hi. Nice to meet you.
- Hi. Nice to meet you.

21:53.020 --> 21:55.689
Yeah, that's Cassie Sheppard
and Josie Radek.

21:55.856 --> 21:57.233
- Hi.
- Hi. Nice to meet you.

21:57.399 --> 21:59.068
Do you want to have a seat?

21:59.693 --> 22:00.736
Thank you.

22:00.861 --> 22:02.863
So, first day
at the Southern Reach.

22:02.947 --> 22:04.031
Yes.

22:05.533 --> 22:07.201
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

22:07.910 --> 22:09.411
You all been here a long time?

22:10.621 --> 22:12.248
Yeah, right from the start.

22:12.414 --> 22:13.749
I'm a geomorphologist.

22:13.874 --> 22:17.044
I've been testing the magnetic
fields around the boundary.

22:17.211 --> 22:20.506
Which is like using confetti
to test a hurricane.

22:21.090 --> 22:23.551
And I've been here

22:23.717 --> 22:26.262
10 months? Ten months!

22:26.387 --> 22:27.847
Paramedic from Chicago.

22:27.930 --> 22:29.557
Tried to join an NGO, but
my application got flagged,

22:29.640 --> 22:31.433
so Southern Reach got me.

22:31.725 --> 22:32.726
Only two months.

22:33.060 --> 22:34.103
I'm a physicist.

22:34.228 --> 22:36.897
I came straight from
my Cambridge post-doc.

22:37.106 --> 22:38.607
She's very smart.

22:39.400 --> 22:41.068
What's your story, Lena?

22:41.235 --> 22:43.487
I'm from Johns Hopkins.
Biologist.

22:43.612 --> 22:45.322
- There you go.
- Biologist?

22:45.447 --> 22:46.782
- Told you she was smart.
- What?

22:46.949 --> 22:48.158
We had a bet on your profession,

22:48.284 --> 22:50.286
and Josie had "biologist,"
of course.

22:52.830 --> 22:55.332
- I had "law enforcement."
- I had you as single.

22:55.457 --> 22:58.127
Jesus! Do you have to hit on
everyone, like all the time?

22:58.210 --> 22:59.712
Come on. Fuck that.
Under the circumstances,

22:59.795 --> 23:02.298
I think I'm allowed to roll
the dice a few more times.

23:03.215 --> 23:04.800
Under what circumstances?

23:07.636 --> 23:10.764
Well, yeah, crazy as it seems...

23:11.098 --> 23:13.267
Crazy as it is.

23:15.603 --> 23:17.771
We are headed that way.

23:22.484 --> 23:23.944
You're going into the Shimmer?

23:24.028 --> 23:25.237
Six days and counting.

23:27.281 --> 23:28.991
- You three?
- Four.

23:29.491 --> 23:30.492
Ventress.

23:32.161 --> 23:33.162
Dr. Ventress?

23:33.287 --> 23:35.289
Team leader.

23:36.290 --> 23:38.125
- All women.
- Scientists.

23:38.292 --> 23:41.211
The previous teams have been
largely military, so yeah.

23:43.172 --> 23:44.632
What do you think
happened to them?

23:45.174 --> 23:46.759
Well, there are two theories

23:46.842 --> 23:48.677
of what went wrong
in the Shimmer.

23:49.011 --> 23:50.971
One, something kills them.

23:51.055 --> 23:53.682
Two, they go crazy
and kill each other.

23:55.476 --> 23:57.519
There was one military
guy who made it out.

23:57.603 --> 23:58.646
Yeah.

23:59.021 --> 24:00.022
Sergeant.

24:00.147 --> 24:02.358
Yeah, but you heard about
the state that he was in.

24:50.531 --> 24:51.532
Kane,

24:54.535 --> 24:56.704
I know why you went in.

25:05.546 --> 25:07.256
I am so sorry.

25:09.717 --> 25:11.885
And I know what I have to do.

25:15.597 --> 25:17.266
So, you didn't tell
them about your connection

25:17.391 --> 25:18.934
to Sergeant Kane.

25:19.268 --> 25:22.271
I thought
it would complicate things.

25:22.896 --> 25:23.897
What?

25:24.940 --> 25:26.775
What would it complicate?

25:33.073 --> 25:35.325
Why are you going
into the Shimmer?

25:37.244 --> 25:39.329
The mission statement is to

25:39.455 --> 25:42.833
reach the supposed source of
the Shimmer, the lighthouse.

25:42.958 --> 25:46.962
Enter, acquire data, and return.

25:48.756 --> 25:51.759
But I don't think that
that's your mission statement.

25:57.097 --> 25:58.432
No.

26:06.315 --> 26:09.985
I've been watching the
phenomenon for a while now.

26:10.360 --> 26:12.946
I profile the volunteers.

26:13.989 --> 26:16.325
I pick the teams.

26:18.160 --> 26:21.163
They enter. I watch.

26:23.665 --> 26:25.834
I watch it grow closer.

26:28.962 --> 26:31.090
There's only so long
one can do that.

26:33.008 --> 26:35.010
But you need to know
what's inside?

26:36.678 --> 26:38.555
Yes. I do.

26:41.642 --> 26:42.976
So do I.

26:44.144 --> 26:45.771
So that's the complication.

26:47.523 --> 26:48.774
You want to come with us.

26:50.317 --> 26:52.277
I can't do anything
for him here.

26:54.196 --> 26:55.572
Soldier-scientist.

26:56.990 --> 27:00.661
You can fight. You can learn.

27:03.247 --> 27:04.706
You can save him.

27:11.004 --> 27:12.965
You requested to join
the mission.

27:13.590 --> 27:15.467
You knew all
other missions had failed,

27:15.551 --> 27:18.512
and the only survivor
was barely surviving.

27:19.513 --> 27:20.764
That was a brave choice.

27:21.890 --> 27:23.058
Lowed him.

27:25.352 --> 27:27.521
I'm only trying to understand
what drove you.

27:31.024 --> 27:32.151
Lowed him.

27:35.028 --> 27:36.280
So I went in.

30:20.694 --> 30:22.863
And then we get some real meals.

30:23.238 --> 30:26.742
Spaghetti. Here's Radek's
vegetable crackers.

30:28.910 --> 30:31.038
Cornbread. That's not so bad.

30:31.705 --> 30:33.373
You're finally awake.

30:33.623 --> 30:36.710
Got to give me a second.
I'm a little disoriented.

30:37.044 --> 30:38.420
Join the club.

30:38.754 --> 30:41.089
You don't remember
setting up camp, do you?

30:43.091 --> 30:44.760
I don't remember anything

30:45.218 --> 30:47.054
after we reached the tree line.

30:48.180 --> 30:49.181
None of us do.

30:50.057 --> 30:51.767
And we did a food inventory.

30:51.892 --> 30:54.603
From the depletion, it looks
like we've been out here for

30:54.728 --> 30:56.772
at least three or four days.

30:58.231 --> 30:59.358
That's not possible.

30:59.983 --> 31:01.443
That's what I said.

31:03.445 --> 31:07.741
Guys, I've been checking
my comms and nav equipment.

31:08.241 --> 31:10.327
They boot up fine, no problem
with the electronics,

31:10.452 --> 31:11.953
and the camera is working,

31:12.079 --> 31:14.915
but anything that sends
a signal out of the Shimmer

31:14.998 --> 31:16.249
is down.

31:16.625 --> 31:18.585
Even though we've probably
got about 20 satellites

31:18.668 --> 31:21.296
above us right now.
And check this out.

31:24.841 --> 31:26.468
So we have got

31:26.551 --> 31:29.388
no compass, no comms,
no coordinates,

31:30.222 --> 31:31.348
and no landmarks.

31:31.473 --> 31:33.308
Well, we know
we're in the state park.

31:33.433 --> 31:36.603
We head south, hit the ocean,
then just follow the shoreline

31:36.686 --> 31:37.687
until we hit the perimeter wall.

31:37.813 --> 31:38.855
Right?

31:39.940 --> 31:40.941
How do we know what's south?

31:41.024 --> 31:42.651
Come on, Josie, you know this.

31:43.193 --> 31:44.653
Hour hand at the sun.

31:45.987 --> 31:48.156
Split the difference between
the hour hand and 12.

31:48.323 --> 31:49.324
South.

31:49.699 --> 31:52.411
Good. We're oriented.

31:52.702 --> 31:53.870
We weren't really expecting

31:53.995 --> 31:55.956
the comms equipment to work,
were we?

31:56.331 --> 31:57.999
I mean, there's been
three years of expeditions

31:58.083 --> 31:59.876
and three years
of radio silence.

32:01.002 --> 32:03.130
Let's pack up and get moving.

32:03.630 --> 32:05.549
We've already lost
a lot of the day.

33:06.234 --> 33:07.319
I'm gonna check this out.

33:07.402 --> 33:09.112
Get us out of this damn swamp.

33:09.237 --> 33:10.238
All right.

33:10.864 --> 33:12.282
Let's check out the hut.

33:30.842 --> 33:33.512
Looks like someone's about
to have a wedding.

33:35.931 --> 33:38.058
These are very strange.

33:39.100 --> 33:40.560
Why?

33:41.978 --> 33:44.064
They're all so different.

33:44.147 --> 33:45.607
To look at them,
you wouldn't say

33:45.690 --> 33:47.859
that they're the same species.

33:48.944 --> 33:50.946
But they're growing from
the same branch structure.

33:52.280 --> 33:54.824
So it has to be
the same species.

33:54.950 --> 33:56.535
It's the same plant.

33:57.619 --> 34:00.247
It's like they're stuck
in a continuous mutation.

34:00.330 --> 34:01.498
A pathology?

34:02.791 --> 34:03.875
Yeah, well,

34:05.544 --> 34:07.379
you'd sure as hell
call it a pathology

34:07.462 --> 34:09.297
if you saw this in a human.

34:19.724 --> 34:21.101
Jackpot

34:21.810 --> 34:22.894
Sheppard.

34:23.520 --> 34:24.604
Mode of transportation.

34:29.734 --> 34:31.194
Anything interesting in there?

34:31.486 --> 34:34.489
No. It's been long abandoned,
maybe even before...

34:35.907 --> 34:36.992
Radek?

34:38.243 --> 34:39.494
Radek!

34:40.203 --> 34:42.664
- Radek!
- It's got my bag!

34:42.747 --> 34:44.040
Radek!

34:47.335 --> 34:49.504
Something's got my bag!

34:51.172 --> 34:52.674
It's got my bag!

34:57.429 --> 34:59.598
- Josie, what's happening?
- What's going on?

35:01.182 --> 35:02.642
Grab my shoulder!

35:05.687 --> 35:07.397
Get her. Come on.

35:08.940 --> 35:10.108
I got her!

35:13.028 --> 35:14.154
You're good. You're good.

35:14.696 --> 35:15.989
Okay.

35:22.871 --> 35:25.498
Let's sit you down.
Help me with her bag.

35:25.582 --> 35:28.043
Okay, just breathe.
It's okay, you're just fine.

35:28.168 --> 35:30.337
- What the hell happened?
- Something in the water.

35:41.890 --> 35:43.600
Get up! Get up! Go.

35:53.443 --> 35:55.195
Shit! Get back.

35:59.908 --> 36:00.909
Sheppard!

36:01.326 --> 36:02.744
Sheppard, watch out!

36:06.331 --> 36:07.749
Holy fuck!

36:52.210 --> 36:54.462
It's exactly the same
as the flowers.

36:55.797 --> 36:56.840
Look at the teeth.

36:58.299 --> 36:59.801
Concentric rows.

37:00.802 --> 37:03.763
Something here is making giant
waves in the gene pool.

37:04.139 --> 37:05.807
Sharks have teeth like that,
don't they?

37:05.890 --> 37:08.143
Do you think it's a crossbreed?

37:09.310 --> 37:12.731
You can't crossbreed
between different species.

37:15.900 --> 37:17.444
Lena, this is getting heavy.

37:27.245 --> 37:29.706
The mutations
were subtle at first.

37:30.915 --> 37:34.169
More extreme as we grew
closer to the lighthouse.

37:35.837 --> 37:37.839
Corruptions of form.

37:39.048 --> 37:40.675
Duplicates of form.

37:41.009 --> 37:42.343
Duplicates?

37:45.597 --> 37:46.723
Echoes.

37:51.019 --> 37:53.897
Is it possible
these were hallucinations?

37:55.857 --> 37:57.817
I wondered that myself.

37:59.194 --> 38:01.404
But they were shared
among all of us.

38:03.782 --> 38:05.366
It was dreamlike.

38:07.035 --> 38:08.369
Nightmarish?

38:08.870 --> 38:10.079
Not always.

38:12.373 --> 38:14.542
Sometimes it was beautiful.

38:42.779 --> 38:44.113
You hurt?

38:44.322 --> 38:46.241
It's just a bruise.

38:47.242 --> 38:49.577
Must have gotten that
from the gator.

38:50.078 --> 38:51.162
Yeah.

38:55.959 --> 38:58.002
So, where'd you learn to shoot?

39:00.171 --> 39:02.674
I was in the military
before I was an academic.

39:03.758 --> 39:04.759
Marines?

39:05.051 --> 39:06.761
Army. Seven years.

39:07.428 --> 39:09.305
Feels like a lifetime ago now.

39:09.764 --> 39:10.765
Yeah.

39:12.183 --> 39:14.686
All other lives
feel like a lifetime ago.

39:15.144 --> 39:17.272
We were kids, I was married.

39:18.606 --> 39:20.441
Which do you carry
around your neck?

39:20.525 --> 39:22.277
A husband or a child?

39:22.527 --> 39:23.695
Husband.

39:24.946 --> 39:28.867
He was in the Army, too.
That's... That's how we met.

39:29.659 --> 39:31.286
"Was" in the Army? He quit?

39:33.121 --> 39:34.122
K.l.A.

39:36.207 --> 39:37.709
I'm sorry to hear that.

39:39.168 --> 39:41.254
Guess there had to be something.

39:41.337 --> 39:42.630
What do you mean?

39:44.883 --> 39:47.385
Volunteering for this.

39:47.468 --> 39:50.138
It's not exactly something
you do if your life is in

39:50.221 --> 39:51.723
perfect harmony.

39:53.933 --> 39:55.560
We're all damaged goods here.

39:56.728 --> 39:58.229
Anya is sober,

39:58.563 --> 40:00.064
therefore an addict.

40:00.231 --> 40:02.317
And Josie wears long sleeves

40:02.400 --> 40:03.484
because she doesn't
want you to see

40:03.610 --> 40:05.153
the scars on her forearms.

40:05.236 --> 40:06.905
She's tried to kill herself?

40:07.488 --> 40:10.158
No, I think the opposite.
Trying to feel alive.

40:13.328 --> 40:14.329
Ventress?

40:15.371 --> 40:17.832
Yeah. As far as anyone knows,

40:18.917 --> 40:22.795
no friends, no family,
no partner, no children.

40:24.005 --> 40:25.840
No concession in her at all.

40:28.551 --> 40:29.552
You'?

40:30.470 --> 40:32.013
I also lost someone.

40:34.599 --> 40:36.225
Not a husband, though.

40:36.726 --> 40:39.020
A daughter. Leukemia.

40:40.104 --> 40:41.397
God, I'm sorry.

40:42.190 --> 40:43.900
In a way, it's two bereavements.

40:45.860 --> 40:48.738
My beautiful girl

40:50.531 --> 40:52.075
and the person I once was.

40:52.200 --> 40:53.368
Hey, hey.

40:54.118 --> 40:55.787
We got something here.

41:27.151 --> 41:28.403
This used to be the headquarters

41:28.486 --> 41:29.988
of the Southern Reach

41:30.989 --> 41:32.782
before the Shimmer swallowed it.

41:36.327 --> 41:37.704
More mutations.

41:38.746 --> 41:40.164
They're everywhere.

41:40.832 --> 41:42.166
Malignant.

41:42.834 --> 41:44.419
Like tumors.

41:46.004 --> 41:47.714
Is that the old mess hall?

41:47.797 --> 41:48.798
Yeah.

41:48.923 --> 41:51.259
Let's billet there. Come on.

42:26.878 --> 42:29.756
There's beds and bags.
You think people are here?

42:30.798 --> 42:31.966
Were here.

42:32.967 --> 42:34.802
Yeah, I'm gonna go
with the past tense.

42:55.740 --> 42:56.741
Damn.

43:02.997 --> 43:04.499
Shit.

43:14.008 --> 43:16.761
This shit is heavy.
Can't carry this.

43:33.236 --> 43:34.612
Lena, what you got going on?

43:36.614 --> 43:38.199
Guys, check this out.

43:40.118 --> 43:42.620
Peyton. Mayer.

43:44.288 --> 43:46.666
Kane. Shelley.

43:46.999 --> 43:49.377
Those were the soldiers
on the last expedition.

43:49.627 --> 43:50.878
Looks like they
were using this room

43:51.003 --> 43:52.547
as their base of operations.

43:52.630 --> 43:54.423
Why are some of the names
crossed out?

43:54.549 --> 43:56.134
Let's not jump to conclusions.

43:56.217 --> 43:57.426
I don't know, maybe we should.

43:57.635 --> 43:58.719
Yeah.

43:59.137 --> 44:00.721
This is a plan-view
of the base, right?

44:00.847 --> 44:02.390
Yep. This is the mess hall.

44:02.515 --> 44:03.891
- That's the building we're in?
- Yep.

44:04.016 --> 44:05.434
I think that the times
by the names

44:05.560 --> 44:07.145
are a guard rota,

44:07.478 --> 44:09.522
so if they were guarding the
perimeter, we should, too.

44:09.605 --> 44:11.482
- Copy that.
- Yep.

44:24.328 --> 44:26.664
This might be able
to tell us something.

44:30.251 --> 44:32.587
"For those that follow."

44:33.588 --> 44:36.424
I believe that means us.

44:44.932 --> 44:46.601
Memory card.

44:48.769 --> 44:50.646
I should be able to play this.

44:58.112 --> 44:59.447
It's working.

45:03.868 --> 45:04.869
All right?

45:10.541 --> 45:12.460
- Okay?
- Okay.

45:12.543 --> 45:13.586
Okay.

45:23.721 --> 45:26.057
- Okay. Okay. Okay.
- Okay.

45:26.390 --> 45:27.725
Ready? Okay.

45:42.573 --> 45:43.908
Shit.

45:44.450 --> 45:45.952
What is he doing?

45:53.417 --> 45:56.754
No, stop, stop,
stop, stop, stop.

45:57.922 --> 45:59.215
Hold him. Hold him down.

46:03.761 --> 46:05.513
There. There.

46:21.862 --> 46:23.572
Okay. So we know what happened
to the last group,

46:23.698 --> 46:24.865
they went insane.

46:25.866 --> 46:27.368
There was something
alive inside that man.

46:27.451 --> 46:28.953
No, that was a trick
of the light.

46:29.036 --> 46:30.037
What?

46:30.162 --> 46:31.497
I've been a paramedic
for 10 years. All right?

46:31.580 --> 46:33.207
I've scraped people
off the side of the road.

46:33.291 --> 46:36.168
You see some weird shit.
That was a trick of the light.

46:36.252 --> 46:37.420
His insides were moving.

46:37.545 --> 46:40.131
No, it was shock, Radek.
That was a shock response.

46:40.214 --> 46:41.215
Watch it again.

46:41.340 --> 46:42.717
No, I'm not gonna
fucking watch it again!

46:42.842 --> 46:44.885
That was not intestines.
It was like a worm.

46:44.969 --> 46:46.887
Okay, then you
watch it, Sheppard!

46:51.142 --> 46:52.476
Where are you going?

47:06.657 --> 47:08.826
- Where'd she go?
- Just ahead.

48:05.257 --> 48:06.425
What is it?

48:07.385 --> 48:08.469
I don't know.

48:26.612 --> 48:27.780
I don't want
to stay here tonight.

48:27.863 --> 48:29.281
We don't have a choice.

48:31.409 --> 48:33.077
- Please.
- Come on.

48:33.160 --> 48:36.038
It's too late in the day
for us to move on.

48:36.330 --> 48:37.832
Come on, let's go outside.

49:19.498 --> 49:22.042
That's nice of you.

49:24.295 --> 49:26.380
Why aren't you here?

49:28.466 --> 49:30.134
I got to leave a day early.

49:30.634 --> 49:31.719
What?

49:32.887 --> 49:34.096
Wait, today?

49:35.806 --> 49:37.558
- Right now.
- Shit.

49:38.225 --> 49:39.852
But we had a whole day planned.

49:39.935 --> 49:42.313
We were gonna drive
to the country.

49:42.897 --> 49:44.940
- We can't.
- Can you at least...

49:50.613 --> 49:51.947
"Now" means right now?

49:55.659 --> 49:56.660
Yeah.

49:59.955 --> 50:01.207
What is it?

50:08.339 --> 50:09.507
I do

50:13.385 --> 50:14.470
love you,

50:15.429 --> 50:16.430
Lena.

50:18.849 --> 50:19.975
I love you, too.

51:17.241 --> 51:18.325
Hey.

51:20.077 --> 51:21.579
The mystery unraveling?

51:23.414 --> 51:25.332
Something's unraveling.

51:26.333 --> 51:27.960
I think you're doing okay.

51:30.254 --> 51:31.839
Look, Josie's getting some rest.

51:31.964 --> 51:32.965
Yeah.

51:33.048 --> 51:34.925
With the help
of a little sedative.

51:35.134 --> 51:37.553
How about you? Get some sleep?

51:38.345 --> 51:39.430
Some.

51:40.264 --> 51:42.474
I'm at least
as freaked as Josie.

51:43.934 --> 51:45.811
I'm just hiding it better.

51:49.481 --> 51:50.941
I should check on Ventress.

51:52.776 --> 51:53.777
Yep.

52:25.267 --> 52:26.268
What are you doing up?

52:26.393 --> 52:28.062
You're not supposed
to relieve me until 3:00.

52:28.145 --> 52:30.105
I'm done sleeping for the night.

52:30.648 --> 52:31.899
Okay.

52:33.275 --> 52:34.777
Come look at this.

52:38.072 --> 52:39.448
Okay, this is where we are,

52:41.033 --> 52:42.576
and that's the lighthouse.

52:42.910 --> 52:44.870
Southwest is Ville Perdu.

52:44.953 --> 52:47.790
It's a small community
we evacuated two years ago.

52:48.499 --> 52:51.335
I think we should
head there tomorrow,

52:51.669 --> 52:53.087
and then head out for the coast

52:53.170 --> 52:55.005
the following morning.

52:57.800 --> 52:58.801
Good.

53:03.681 --> 53:04.682
You Okay?

53:11.313 --> 53:12.981
I was gonna say, when

53:13.565 --> 53:16.110
you didn't tell the team
about your connection to Kane,

53:16.193 --> 53:18.195
I wasn't sure
if that was a good idea.

53:20.656 --> 53:22.783
But after seeing that footage,

53:25.911 --> 53:26.912
yeah...

53:27.705 --> 53:29.873
I'm not sure how they would
have reacted to you.

53:32.835 --> 53:35.254
Why did my husband volunteer
for a suicide mission?

53:35.921 --> 53:37.381
Is that what you think
we're doing?

53:38.257 --> 53:39.341
Committing suicide?

53:39.508 --> 53:42.177
You must have profiled him,
you must have assessed him.

53:43.262 --> 53:44.805
He must have said something.

53:46.473 --> 53:49.101
So you're asking me
as a psychologist?

53:50.352 --> 53:51.353
Yeah.

53:52.688 --> 53:54.481
Then as a psychologist,

53:55.441 --> 53:59.111
I'd say you're confusing
suicide with self-destruction.

54:01.530 --> 54:03.782
Almost none of us commit suicide

54:04.533 --> 54:06.493
and almost all of us
self-destruct.

54:07.035 --> 54:09.747
In some way,
in some part of our lives.

54:11.123 --> 54:13.500
We drink, or we smoke.

54:14.126 --> 54:16.336
We destabilize the good job

54:18.630 --> 54:20.007
or the happy marriage.

54:25.137 --> 54:26.972
But these aren't decisions,
they're...

54:28.056 --> 54:29.349
They're impulses.

54:29.641 --> 54:30.726
In fact,

54:31.560 --> 54:33.103
you're probably better equipped

54:33.187 --> 54:35.481
- to explain this than I am.
- What does that mean?

54:36.648 --> 54:37.983
You're a biologist.

54:39.318 --> 54:41.737
Isn't self-destruction
coded into us?

54:42.237 --> 54:43.739
Programed into each cell?

54:46.617 --> 54:47.826
What was that?

54:48.160 --> 54:49.411
Don't know.

55:01.173 --> 55:02.174
Josie, wake up.

55:02.257 --> 55:03.425
Wake up, Josie, come on.
Wake up.

55:03.550 --> 55:04.593
Something's happening.

55:05.010 --> 55:06.762
- Do you see anything?
- No.

55:07.095 --> 55:08.931
What happened? I heard a noise.

55:10.390 --> 55:11.642
What?

55:14.269 --> 55:15.771
Something's come through
the fence.

55:16.855 --> 55:17.856
Through the fence?

55:17.940 --> 55:19.608
It's ripped open
like a fucking zipper.

55:25.113 --> 55:27.449
- I can't see anything.
- Yeah, neither can I.

55:29.868 --> 55:31.036
Sheppard!

55:31.620 --> 55:32.621
Sheppard!

55:32.746 --> 55:34.414
- Fuck.
- What's going on?

55:34.498 --> 55:36.667
Sheppard was just next to me,
and something took her.

55:37.709 --> 55:39.628
Fuck! Fuck!

55:39.795 --> 55:41.547
- Sheppard!
- Shit.

55:43.882 --> 55:45.384
Help me!

55:46.385 --> 55:47.886
Help me!

55:53.308 --> 55:54.601
Sheppard!

55:59.064 --> 56:00.315
Sheppard!

56:29.761 --> 56:32.598
We have to go back.
We have to go back now.

56:32.764 --> 56:33.849
She's right.

56:34.016 --> 56:35.642
Right? In what sense?

56:35.809 --> 56:37.436
We've been attacked twice.

56:37.978 --> 56:39.521
We lost one of our own.

56:39.646 --> 56:41.440
We have evidence
the previous team

56:41.523 --> 56:42.649
went nuts and chopped
each other up.

56:42.774 --> 56:45.277
I really don't know how much
more right she has to be.

56:45.360 --> 56:46.862
We haven't reached
the lighthouse.

56:47.029 --> 56:48.322
We still don't
understand the cause

56:48.447 --> 56:49.656
or the nature of the Shimmer.

56:49.823 --> 56:51.408
We have data,
observations, photographs.

56:51.491 --> 56:52.492
She has hella footage.

56:52.618 --> 56:54.244
All of which
makes the phenomenon

56:54.328 --> 56:55.621
less explicable, not more.

56:58.707 --> 57:00.334
I'm gonna get to the lighthouse.

57:00.459 --> 57:02.336
And I'm fine going on my own.

57:02.419 --> 57:04.379
You just need to decide

57:05.088 --> 57:06.924
whether you're coming
with me or not.

57:18.644 --> 57:21.146
It's like she doesn't even
notice that Sheppard is dead.

57:21.229 --> 57:24.483
She's crazy.
She's a crazy old bitch.

57:25.484 --> 57:27.110
And thanks for
the fucking backup, Lena!

57:29.154 --> 57:30.447
I didn't realize
there were sides.

57:30.530 --> 57:31.531
Yeah.

57:31.740 --> 57:32.908
Yeah, there are sides.

57:34.034 --> 57:37.037
Okay. Then I agree with you,
we should go back.

57:37.663 --> 57:39.039
Good. Okay, great. There we go.

57:39.164 --> 57:40.624
Okay, so the three of us

57:40.707 --> 57:42.334
- can just pack up our...
- Hold on a minute.

57:42.542 --> 57:43.627
Hold on. We should go back, yes.

57:43.710 --> 57:46.171
But it took us, what,
six days to get here?

57:46.338 --> 57:49.091
And the coast is two days away.

57:49.675 --> 57:52.177
And as Sheppard said,

57:52.886 --> 57:53.887
when we get to the coast,

57:54.012 --> 57:56.556
we can just follow it until
we hit the perimeter wall.

57:56.932 --> 57:58.767
You're saying that we get out
by going deeper in?

57:59.226 --> 58:00.227
Yeah, if you like. Yeah.

58:00.310 --> 58:01.603
"Like"?

58:01.770 --> 58:04.523
No, I don't fucking "like."

58:08.694 --> 58:10.028
This isn't some bullshit tactic

58:10.112 --> 58:11.363
to get us to the lighthouse,
is it?

58:11.530 --> 58:14.199
This is not about
the lighthouse, okay?

58:14.700 --> 58:16.868
I believe that the coast
is the best route out.

58:21.665 --> 58:22.666
Okay?

58:35.887 --> 58:37.097
You lied to them.

58:40.475 --> 58:42.811
I didn't know
what going back meant.

58:43.145 --> 58:45.689
Why it would be safer
than going forward.

58:46.815 --> 58:47.899
You didn't know,

58:47.983 --> 58:50.318
but you made the decision
to continue as if you did.

58:50.485 --> 58:51.987
Ventress made the decision.

58:52.070 --> 58:55.282
Ventress had cancer,
she was never coming back.

58:56.241 --> 58:57.784
You knew she was sick.

58:58.535 --> 58:59.619
I had guessed.

59:02.748 --> 59:04.332
And you wanted to continue?

59:06.668 --> 59:07.753
Yes.

59:08.837 --> 59:10.005
I did.

59:57.135 --> 59:58.595
She could still be alive.

59:58.804 --> 01:00:00.263
It's highly doubtful.

01:00:01.807 --> 01:00:03.391
We need to know.

01:00:06.019 --> 01:00:07.020
Go.

01:00:07.979 --> 01:00:08.980
Fine.

01:00:11.274 --> 01:00:12.526
I'm coming with you.

01:00:13.902 --> 01:00:15.153
I'll go alone.

01:02:44.177 --> 01:02:45.303
Did you find her?

01:02:45.971 --> 01:02:46.972
Yeah.

01:02:48.306 --> 01:02:49.349
She's dead.

01:03:13.999 --> 01:03:15.333
You Okay?

01:03:16.084 --> 01:03:17.294
Fine.

01:03:17.377 --> 01:03:19.546
Just leave me the fuck alone.

01:03:45.780 --> 01:03:47.449
We'll camp here tonight.

01:03:48.450 --> 01:03:51.202
It's another two hours' walk
up the coast.

01:04:28.823 --> 01:04:30.575
They've grown this way.

01:04:31.409 --> 01:04:33.078
That doesn't make any sense.

01:04:33.745 --> 01:04:35.246
I think it does.

01:04:44.130 --> 01:04:45.757
At first, I thought
the radio waves

01:04:45.840 --> 01:04:47.592
were blocked by the Shimmer,

01:04:47.759 --> 01:04:49.844
and that's why no one
inside could communicate

01:04:49.969 --> 01:04:52.180
with base or GPS.

01:04:53.181 --> 01:04:55.141
But the light waves
aren't blocked,

01:04:55.225 --> 01:04:57.685
they're refracted. And...

01:05:02.023 --> 01:05:04.109
It's the same with the radios.

01:05:04.776 --> 01:05:06.820
Signals aren't gone.

01:05:06.903 --> 01:05:08.613
They're scrambled.

01:05:14.285 --> 01:05:16.121
That leaf in your hand.

01:05:16.913 --> 01:05:18.998
Do you know what you'd get
if you sequenced it?

01:05:19.624 --> 01:05:20.625
What?

01:05:21.084 --> 01:05:23.837
- Human Hox genes.
- "Hox"? What does "Hox" mean?

01:05:24.587 --> 01:05:26.464
They're the genes
that define the body plan,

01:05:26.548 --> 01:05:28.091
the physical structure.

01:05:30.885 --> 01:05:33.054
And the plants
have human body plan.

01:05:33.179 --> 01:05:37.434
Arms attached to shoulders,
legs to hips.

01:05:37.559 --> 01:05:39.185
It's literally not possible.

01:05:39.644 --> 01:05:41.396
It's literally what's happening.

01:05:43.731 --> 01:05:45.483
The Shimmer is a prism,

01:05:45.733 --> 01:05:47.485
but it refracts everything.

01:05:48.153 --> 01:05:50.697
Not just light and radio waves.

01:05:51.322 --> 01:05:54.325
Animal DNA. Plant DNA.

01:05:55.535 --> 01:05:56.870
All DNA.

01:05:57.120 --> 01:05:58.788
What do you mean, all DNA?

01:05:59.497 --> 01:06:01.666
She's talking about our DNA.

01:06:04.085 --> 01:06:05.753
She's talking about us.

01:07:12.403 --> 01:07:14.989
All right.
I guess this is the bedroom.

01:07:16.407 --> 01:07:18.368
Let's secure doors and windows.

01:08:44.078 --> 01:08:45.538
This was a mistake.

01:08:48.166 --> 01:08:49.334
Okay.

01:08:55.715 --> 01:08:58.384
You spend more time away from
your husband than with him.

01:09:00.470 --> 01:09:01.888
You can't talk to him
about work,

01:09:01.971 --> 01:09:03.222
and he won't talk
to you about his.

01:09:03.681 --> 01:09:05.266
And there is a clear physical

01:09:05.391 --> 01:09:07.185
and intellectual connection
between us.

01:09:07.560 --> 01:09:08.645
Have I covered the bases?

01:09:08.728 --> 01:09:09.896
You forgot to mention your wife.

01:09:09.979 --> 01:09:11.230
I love my wife.

01:09:13.941 --> 01:09:15.401
She's blameless in this.

01:09:24.202 --> 01:09:25.286
Come on, Lena.

01:09:26.579 --> 01:09:28.081
What's really going on here?

01:09:30.375 --> 01:09:32.752
You think that something
may have happened to him?

01:09:37.799 --> 01:09:39.258
Or you think he knows.

01:09:41.969 --> 01:09:43.137
That's it, isn't it?

01:09:43.971 --> 01:09:46.766
You think somehow he's found
out about our affair.

01:09:48.810 --> 01:09:50.186
Has he found out?

01:09:51.145 --> 01:09:52.271
Yes.

01:09:55.817 --> 01:09:56.943
You should go.

01:09:59.153 --> 01:10:00.822
- No, Lena, I...
- Dan.

01:10:01.656 --> 01:10:03.741
I'm not interested in talking,

01:10:04.117 --> 01:10:05.993
or anything you have to say.

01:10:06.828 --> 01:10:08.496
Just get dressed and get out.

01:10:11.207 --> 01:10:12.625
You know, it's not me you hate.

01:10:12.709 --> 01:10:14.085
It's yourself.

01:10:17.338 --> 01:10:18.756
No, Dan, it's you, too.

01:10:22.844 --> 01:10:24.595
It's never gonna happen again.

01:10:30.852 --> 01:10:31.978
You lying bitch!

01:10:33.479 --> 01:10:35.398
- What's going on?
- No.

01:10:35.982 --> 01:10:37.817
You don't get to ask
that fucking question.

01:10:37.942 --> 01:10:39.360
You answer it!

01:11:08.514 --> 01:11:09.682
Brother.

01:11:11.768 --> 01:11:12.769
Boyfriend.

01:11:14.687 --> 01:11:15.688
Husband.

01:11:19.609 --> 01:11:20.818
Husband.

01:11:23.112 --> 01:11:24.739
Why didn't you tell us?

01:11:27.158 --> 01:11:28.159
You knew.

01:11:29.327 --> 01:11:30.536
Obviously.

01:11:34.791 --> 01:11:35.792
Did you know?

01:11:40.505 --> 01:11:41.506
Okay.

01:11:45.927 --> 01:11:46.928
So, there are two theories

01:11:47.053 --> 01:11:48.137
of what went wrong
in the Shimmer.

01:11:48.221 --> 01:11:50.807
One is that something in here
killed them. Two

01:11:51.390 --> 01:11:53.726
is that they went crazy
and they killed each other.

01:11:55.561 --> 01:11:57.688
Josie nearly got killed
by an alligator,

01:11:57.772 --> 01:12:00.233
and Cass did get killed
by a bear.

01:12:02.902 --> 01:12:04.946
So, yes, theory one, it fits.

01:12:08.074 --> 01:12:09.283
But

01:12:11.994 --> 01:12:13.579
I didn't actually see a bear.

01:12:15.122 --> 01:12:16.582
And neither did Josie.

01:12:17.583 --> 01:12:19.669
The only people who saw a bear
were Lena and Ventress.

01:12:20.419 --> 01:12:23.089
So nothing's confirmed.
Everything's on their word.

01:12:23.422 --> 01:12:27.593
Everything's on Lena's word.

01:12:27.844 --> 01:12:29.554
And what we know now...

01:12:30.930 --> 01:12:37.478
What we know
is that Lena is a liar.

01:12:38.104 --> 01:12:40.064
Shut the fuck up!

01:12:41.274 --> 01:12:44.986
Lena, you're a liar.

01:12:47.864 --> 01:12:48.990
Did you kill Cass?

01:12:51.784 --> 01:12:53.536
Did you lose your shit?

01:12:56.289 --> 01:12:57.790
Or do you think
that I've lost my shit,

01:12:57.874 --> 01:12:59.292
and now we're just gonna
fuck each other up?

01:12:59.417 --> 01:13:00.751
That's theory two.

01:13:12.263 --> 01:13:14.265
When I look at my hands

01:13:15.057 --> 01:13:16.517
and my fingerprints,

01:13:18.102 --> 01:13:19.478
I can see them moving.

01:13:26.736 --> 01:13:28.613
If I let you go

01:13:28.821 --> 01:13:31.490
and you tie me to a chair
and cut me open,

01:13:33.159 --> 01:13:36.871
are my insides gonna move
like my fingerprints?

01:13:44.253 --> 01:13:48.007
But I'm not the one
tied to a chair.

01:13:52.511 --> 01:13:53.512
You are.

01:13:58.184 --> 01:13:59.894
Help me!

01:14:02.939 --> 01:14:04.315
Help me!

01:14:04.815 --> 01:14:06.275
Help me!

01:14:06.692 --> 01:14:07.902
Cass?

01:14:10.696 --> 01:14:12.031
You said she was dead.

01:14:13.824 --> 01:14:16.369
Cass! Cass, I'm coming!

01:14:18.204 --> 01:14:20.206
Cass, is that you?

01:15:03.624 --> 01:15:04.750
Help me!

01:15:06.419 --> 01:15:08.587
Help me!

01:15:09.422 --> 01:15:11.424
Help...

01:15:26.355 --> 01:15:27.606
Don't react.

01:15:35.031 --> 01:15:37.324
...me!

01:16:04.393 --> 01:16:06.645
Help...

01:16:20.785 --> 01:16:22.078
...me!

01:17:13.379 --> 01:17:14.380
Help me.

01:17:39.071 --> 01:17:40.739
What are you doing?

01:17:41.031 --> 01:17:43.659
- I'm leaving.
- Now?

01:17:45.411 --> 01:17:48.038
- It's not even light yet.
- I don't have time to wait.

01:17:48.330 --> 01:17:49.957
We are disintegrating!

01:17:50.082 --> 01:17:52.334
Our bodies as fast as
our minds. Can't you feel it?

01:17:53.878 --> 01:17:55.588
It's like the onset of dementia.

01:17:59.008 --> 01:18:00.759
If I don't reach
the lighthouse soon,

01:18:01.260 --> 01:18:02.761
the person
that started this journey

01:18:02.887 --> 01:18:04.430
won't be the person
that ends it.

01:18:05.097 --> 01:18:06.891
I want to be the one
that ends it.

01:19:09.286 --> 01:19:11.247
We should go, Josie.

01:19:18.754 --> 01:19:21.799
How long was your husband
in the Shimmer?

01:19:22.925 --> 01:19:25.135
It's hard to say, exactly.

01:19:27.930 --> 01:19:29.890
Theoretically,
as long as a year.

01:19:32.476 --> 01:19:35.604
That's a long time to be
inside and remain intact.

01:19:36.522 --> 01:19:38.565
I'm not so sure he was intact.

01:19:42.695 --> 01:19:44.071
I'm right

01:19:45.155 --> 01:19:47.950
about the refractions, aren't I?

01:19:48.367 --> 01:19:49.493
Yeah.

01:19:49.618 --> 01:19:51.453
I checked my blood last night.

01:19:54.039 --> 01:19:56.333
It's in me.

01:19:59.503 --> 01:20:01.547
It will be in all of us.

01:20:07.886 --> 01:20:11.432
It was so strange hearing
Sheppard's voice

01:20:11.557 --> 01:20:13.976
in the mouth
of that creature last night.

01:20:15.185 --> 01:20:18.564
I think, as she was dying,
part of her mind became

01:20:19.064 --> 01:20:21.900
part of the creature
that was killing her.

01:20:23.402 --> 01:20:26.196
Imagine dying frightened
and in pain

01:20:26.280 --> 01:20:30.200
and having that as the only
part of you which survives.

01:20:30.909 --> 01:20:32.911
I wouldn't like that at all.

01:20:53.390 --> 01:20:55.434
Ventress wants to face it.

01:20:55.768 --> 01:20:57.603
You want to fight it.

01:20:59.021 --> 01:21:01.899
But I don't think I want
either of those things.

01:21:09.156 --> 01:21:10.282
Josie?

01:21:17.956 --> 01:21:18.957
Josie.

01:21:23.462 --> 01:21:24.797
Josie.

01:21:50.823 --> 01:21:54.785
One by one, all gone,
except you.

01:21:56.995 --> 01:21:58.539
How do you explain that?

01:22:02.459 --> 01:22:04.420
Is it something
I need to explain?

01:22:05.337 --> 01:22:06.797
Yes, you do.

01:22:13.262 --> 01:22:14.680
I had to come back.

01:22:16.515 --> 01:22:18.350
I'm not sure any of them did.

01:22:35.367 --> 01:22:36.535
Hey.

01:22:40.581 --> 01:22:42.040
Hey.

01:27:34.166 --> 01:27:35.792
I thought I was a man.

01:27:43.508 --> 01:27:44.593
I had a life.

01:27:46.845 --> 01:27:48.346
People called me Kane.

01:27:50.849 --> 01:27:52.476
And now I'm not so sure.

01:27:57.355 --> 01:27:59.149
If I wasn't Kane, what was I?

01:28:05.655 --> 01:28:06.782
Was I you?

01:28:10.410 --> 01:28:11.620
Were you me?

01:28:23.507 --> 01:28:27.385
My flesh moves like liquid.

01:28:31.223 --> 01:28:32.307
My mind is

01:28:34.726 --> 01:28:35.936
just cut loose.

01:28:36.728 --> 01:28:37.938
I can't bear it.

01:28:40.607 --> 01:28:42.192
I can't bear it.

01:28:42.609 --> 01:28:44.110
I can't bear it.

01:28:49.241 --> 01:28:51.076
You ever seen
a phosphorus grenade go off?

01:28:53.245 --> 01:28:54.412
They're kinda bright.

01:28:56.373 --> 01:28:57.457
Shield your eyes.

01:28:59.584 --> 01:29:01.878
If you ever get out of here,
you find Lena.

01:29:03.129 --> 01:29:04.297
I will.

01:29:05.090 --> 01:29:06.258
No.

01:29:09.052 --> 01:29:13.723
Five, four, three, two...

01:31:07.587 --> 01:31:10.006
It's the last phase.

01:31:11.675 --> 01:31:14.052
Vanished into havoc.

01:31:17.055 --> 01:31:20.392
Unfathomable mind.

01:31:23.728 --> 01:31:26.481
And now beacon.

01:31:26.564 --> 01:31:28.233
Now sea.

01:31:32.195 --> 01:31:33.863
Dr. Ventress?

01:31:38.952 --> 01:31:40.078
Lena?

01:31:47.627 --> 01:31:49.087
We spoke.

01:31:50.588 --> 01:31:52.257
What was it we said?

01:31:57.846 --> 01:32:00.181
That I needed to know

01:32:00.390 --> 01:32:02.851
what was inside the lighthouse.

01:32:05.311 --> 01:32:06.771
That moment's passed.

01:32:10.608 --> 01:32:12.777
It's inside me now.

01:32:13.778 --> 01:32:16.364
What's inside you?

01:32:16.823 --> 01:32:18.742
It's not like us.

01:32:19.451 --> 01:32:21.786
It's unlike us.

01:32:24.456 --> 01:32:26.458
I don't know what it wants.

01:32:26.916 --> 01:32:28.293
Or if it wants.

01:32:29.294 --> 01:32:31.171
But it will grow

01:32:31.254 --> 01:32:33.965
until it encompasses everything.

01:32:36.384 --> 01:32:38.636
Our bodies and our minds
will be fragmented

01:32:38.720 --> 01:32:40.138
into their smallest parts

01:32:40.263 --> 01:32:44.267
until not one part remains.

01:32:48.146 --> 01:32:49.814
Annihilation.

01:44:08.826 --> 01:44:10.494
So it was alien.

01:44:17.251 --> 01:44:19.086
Can you describe its form?

01:44:23.674 --> 01:44:24.717
No.

01:44:25.509 --> 01:44:27.428
Was it carbon-based or...

01:44:31.223 --> 01:44:32.475
I don't know.

01:44:35.186 --> 01:44:36.520
What did it want?

01:44:38.105 --> 01:44:40.107
I don't think
it wanted anything.

01:44:40.566 --> 01:44:43.110
But it... It attacked you.

01:44:44.028 --> 01:44:45.863
It mirrored me.

01:44:46.363 --> 01:44:47.948
I attacked it.

01:44:48.866 --> 01:44:51.118
I'm not sure it even knew
I was there.

01:44:51.202 --> 01:44:53.370
It came here for a reason.

01:44:54.205 --> 01:44:55.998
It was mutating our environment.

01:44:56.081 --> 01:44:58.042
It was destroying everything.

01:44:59.210 --> 01:45:01.378
It wasn't destroying.

01:45:02.713 --> 01:45:04.757
It was changing everything.

01:45:05.466 --> 01:45:07.968
It was making something new.

01:45:10.721 --> 01:45:12.014
Making what?

01:45:19.897 --> 01:45:21.190
I don't know.

01:45:25.569 --> 01:45:28.489
A team reached the lighthouse
a few hours ago.

01:45:29.323 --> 01:45:30.783
Everything is ash.

01:45:31.575 --> 01:45:34.745
If what you encountered
was once alive,

01:45:35.746 --> 01:45:37.164
it seems it's now dead.

01:45:58.936 --> 01:46:02.231
Now will you tell me
what happened to my husband?

01:46:03.357 --> 01:46:04.859
When the Shimmer disappeared,

01:46:04.942 --> 01:46:06.777
his blood pressure stabilized

01:46:06.861 --> 01:46:09.363
and his pulse rate
started to rise.

01:46:10.739 --> 01:46:12.616
A few hours later,
he was not only awake,

01:46:12.700 --> 01:46:14.118
he was lucid.

01:46:15.619 --> 01:46:18.038
He's still in isolation,
obviously.

01:46:19.123 --> 01:46:20.374
So am I.

01:47:04.209 --> 01:47:05.502
You aren't Kane.

01:47:07.296 --> 01:47:08.505
Are you?

01:47:14.845 --> 01:47:16.138
I don't think so.

01:47:24.355 --> 01:47:25.564
Are you Lena?
